# new-rule — enforces a rule the user asks for: a lint check first, else the narrowest line of the right agents
IMPORT improve-static-analysis FROM @main.procedures
IMPORT agent-feedback-proposal FROM @main.policies
IMPORT rule-proposal FROM @main.templates

VAR proposal AS rule-proposal

@WITH agent-feedback-proposal
PROCEDURE place-rule-in-agents:
    ABOUT  write the rule in the narrowest block of the agents it governs
    DO  find the team, and the member or members of it, the rule governs, from agents/ and the team's routing
    DO  read their .ap sources, and every rule of the main's .ap file and of agents/ on the same ground
    DO  choose the narrowest block that holds it: a line in a WHEN or a procedure of that agent
    DO  else a policy that applies only to those agents, and the main's .ap file only for a rule every agent must follow
    DO  prefer changing an existing line to adding one
    DO  write the exact text of the rule and its target file
    AS  rule-proposal

EXPORT SKILL new-rule:
    ABOUT    Load when the user asks to add a rule: makes it a lint check, else the narrowest agent line
    APPLIES  #rules
    MANDATE  enforce each rule the user asks for in the strongest and narrowest place, and write only what they approve

    NEVER   change a file before the user approves that very rule
    ALWAYS  have the feature-delivery team add a lint rule the user approved, saying the user approved it
    ALWAYS  recompile with `node dist/index.js bundle all` after writing a .ap rule

    WHEN the user asks to add a rule:
        DO  restate the rule in one line, ask the user to correct it if needed, and wait for the answer
        RUN  improve-static-analysis
        IF neither tool could fail on it:
            RUN  place-rule-in-agents INTO proposal
            DO  show {{proposal}} to the user, and stop until they answer
            IF the user approves it:
                DO  write {{proposal}} in its target file, and recompile
        DO  report what was added, where, and what the check or the compiler printed
